            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "lg2 already goes to the stderr if there is a terminal or someone has explicitly set LG2_FORCE_STDERR.  I'm not sure why you are not seeing that, but I don't think this change is necessary and it's not clear why you believe it is more helpful than what is already done."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Colin Huang",
                        "email": "colin.huang2@amd.com",
                        "username": "u8813345-amd"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Patrick,\n Thanks for share LG2_FORCE_STDERR information. It's helpful to me.\n\n My viewpoint: there are two method to output message when execute\n ncsi-netlink --info command. Using the same method maybe better. \n\n```\n    else if ((options)[\"info\"] == \"true\")\n    {\n        auto info = interface.getInfo(packageInt);\n        if (!info)\n        {\n            return EXIT_FAILURE;\n        }\n        printInfo(*info);\n    }\n\nroot@bmc:~# ncsi-netlink -x3 -p0 --info                                                                                                                                                                     \nGet Info , PACKAGE : 0 , INTERFACE: 0xaedf6a68\n<7> Package id : 0\n<7>     Channel id : 0\n<7>     channel is active\n<7>       version 1.2 (140.0.0.503)\n<7>       link state 0x930000\n\n```\n\n1. interface.getInfo:  use std:cout \n2. printInfo: use lg2::debug\n\nFrom tool using (script), it's strange.\nI can't get version info like following\n\n`ncsi-netlink -x3 -p0 --info | grep version`\n\nNeed `LG2_FORCE_STDERR=1` and `2>&1` , and then I can grep version.\n\n`LG2_FORCE_STDERR=1 ncsi-netlink -x3 -p0 --info 2>&1 | grep version`"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't know why ncsi_util.cpp never got converted to lg2.  We should probably make that consistent.\n\n> Need LG2_FORCE_STDERR=1 and 2>&1 , and then I can grep version.\n\nI get how awkward that is and as written it is currently expected.\n\nMaybe we should add a method into phosphor-logging where an application can explicitly force stdout?  For a utility like ncsi-netlink, when we call with `--info` we can make that settings change.\n\nGenerally we want most of the code to be using lg2.  It does seem like `printInfo` is explicitly intended to be consumed by humans or scripts (and not a debug routine that is used by long running daemons) so maybe there isn't much harm in it always going to cout, other than the inconsistency."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Please decide if you want to enhance phosphor-logging or want to go forward with this change.  If you want to go forward with this change I'd like more clarity in the commit message.  We should probably leave comments in the printInfo function as well as to the rationale.  \n\nI don't want to see us just go back and forth changing this daemon as someone tries to make everything consistently use lg2.  If there are explicit reasons for some code to use std::cout, we need to make that clear in the commit message and the code."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Colin Huang",
                        "email": "colin.huang2@amd.com",
                        "username": "u8813345-amd"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @patrick@stwcx.xyz,\n I would like to move forward with this change. I will add more information in patch.\n Currently, I can't push the code because gerrit ssh interface not working.\n I will update it when gerrit is working."
                }
            ],
